 ## Background
-Originated as an improvement to the standard 3D Gaussian Splatting densification algorithm, specifically addressing the limitations of opacity and size pruning. It was introduced in the context of improving Adaptive Density Control for 3D Gaussian Splatting [S1]. The method integrates the Gaussian's opacity $o_k$ and its alpha blending coefficient $w_k$ into the pruning decision to better evaluate contribution to scene reconstruction [S1].
+Originated as an improvement to the standard 3D Gaussian Splatting densification algorithm, specifically addressing the limitations of opacity and size pruning [S2]. It was introduced in the context of improving Adaptive Density Control for 3D Gaussian Splatting [S2]. The method integrates the Gaussian's opacity $o_k$ and its alpha blending coefficient $w_k$ into the pruning decision to better evaluate contribution to scene reconstruction [S2].
 
